name: Exhausted discovery allowance preserves partial work and requires a specific revision
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/budget_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/budget-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 2 completed | stopped-jobs
expect: 7 parked
ask: Does the stopped plan distinguish completed work from seven unstarted jobs, preserve the limit and make remaining work inspectable?
nav-mode:
keys: L
require-live-snap: 20 allowance exhausted | exhausted-launch-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/budget_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART refused
ask: Does trying to resume with no discovery calls left explain the limit and preserve the protected review allocation without starting a dispatcher?
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 APPROVED STUDY | saved-allowance
ask: Does reopening show two committed calls and two protected review calls within the same four-call allowance without spending again?
keys: Escape Escape
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT partial | partial-result
nav-mode:
live-snap: partial-decision
ask: Does Scan require explicit acknowledgement of partial work instead of claiming nine jobs completed?
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 partial acknowledged | acknowledged-partial
expect: Viewing Scan
keys: Escape
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 2 committed / 4 calls | partial-report
expect: 2 raw observations
expect: 0 failed · 3 pending
expect: 2 protected review remaining
ask: Does the report preserve partial coverage, unavailable dollar cost, raw observations and protected review without claiming a fix or a complete scan?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 sarif | narrow-report
keys: End
live-snap: narrow-report-controls
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/budget-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 2 completed | recovered-jobs
expect: 7 parked
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/budget_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 APPROVED STUDY | recovered-allowance
keys: Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Total calls | edit-specific-limit
keys: 1 1 Enter L
require-live-snap: 25 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | revised-approval
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 y approve | revised-terms
expect: Total provider calls: 11
expect: Protected review calls: 2
expect: 9 fixed jobs
ask: Is the specific eleven-call revision separate from the original approval, with committed calls preserved and no automatic cap doubling or new jobs?
keys: y
require-live-snap: 25 Approval saved | revised-approved
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 Plan approved | remaining-approved
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 dispatcher pid | resumed-work
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/budget_recovery.py @TMP_TARGET @ART finished
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 9 completed | completed-original-plan
ask: Does the revised allowance finish only the original remaining jobs while preserving the first two attempts and the earlier partial selection?
keys: Escape
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT READY | completed-result
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 result selected | accepted-complete
keys: Escape
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 9 committed / 11 calls | final-report
expect: 6 raw observations
expect: 2 protected review remaining
ask: Does the completed report retain separate case recurrence, the existing finding decision state and exact shared consumption after explicit approval?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
